hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2941","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Rafi', narrated to us 'Abd al-Razzaq, informed us 'Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Farewell Tawaf (Tawaf al-Wida') on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr), then returned and prayed Zuhr at Mina.

Nafi' (RA) said: ""Ibn 'Umar (RA) used to perform the Farewell Tawaf on the Day of Sacrifice, then return and pray Zuhr at Mina, and he mentioned that the Prophet (ﷺ) did so.""

**CHAPTER:**"
